# Implementation Plan - Fix Certificate Issuance Logic

A discrepancy was found during manual verification: the frontend shows 100% course completion, but the backend rejects the certificate claim due to a mismatched progress model. This plan fixes the `CertificateController` to use the correct `LessonProgress` model from the `Enrollments` module.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The system currently has two progress-tracking models (`CourseProgress` in the `Progress` module and `LessonProgress` in the `Enrollments` module). The frontend and `EnrollmentController` primarily use `LessonProgress`. I am aligning the `Certificates` module to use `LessonProgress` to ensure immediate functionality.

## Proposed Changes

### Certificates Module

#### [MODIFY] [CertificateController.php](file:///d:/learning/SkillPilot/skillpilot-backend/Modules/Certificates/app/Http/Controllers/CertificateController.php)
- Replace usage of `Modules\Progress\Models\CourseProgress` with `Modules\Enrollments\Models\LessonProgress`.
- Update `issue` method logic:
  - Fetch all lesson IDs for the course via `$course->lessons()->pluck('id')`.
  - Count completed lessons by querying `LessonProgress` for those IDs where `is_completed = true`.

#### [MODIFY] [CertificateTest.php](file:///d:/learning/SkillPilot/skillpilot-backend/Modules/Certificates/tests/Feature/CertificateTest.php)
- Update test cases to seed the `lesson_progress` table instead of `course_progress`.
- Ensure the `tenant_id` is correctly included during seeding.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run `php artisan test Modules/Certificates/tests/Feature/CertificateTest.php` to ensure the logic and tests are aligned.

### Manual Verification
- Log in as the student user used in the manual check.
- Attempt to "Claim Certificate" again and verify success.
- Download the generated PDF.
